In article <12SEP199116373876@cc.weber.edu> swillden@cc.weber.edu (Shawn) writes:
>I'm doing some programming on a NeXT and I need to learn a little about
>Objective-C and the NeXT Interface Builder to do it.  The manuals I have are
>the ones that came with the machine and they tell me nothing.  Where could I
>get my hands on some manuals? 

For information on programming in Objective-C in general, you can check out 
a series of articles I wrote for the first three issues of "Object Magazine."  
Although they are tested with Stepstone's version of the compiler, they 
should work with the NeXT version of Objective-C as is.  The important point 
is that the articles document one style for writing reusable applications
in Objective-C.

